oritative game state live, and what should happen after a page refresh or in a second tab? The v1 draft assumes one local game with no isolation but does not commit to whether the Go server or the browser page holds the board. This is observable: with server-held state a refresh resumes the same game, while with page-held state a refresh starts a new game (both are consistent with the criteria above). Recommended default: the server holds a single game's state, a refresh returns the current board, and concurrent requests are serialized. If a reviewer prefers page-held state, that should be confirmed here rather than silently chosen by the implementer.\n- No other material ambiguities were identified for the stated local-game scope. If review surfaces further ambiguity, it will be recorded here rather than turned into a requirement.\n\n## Risk-relevant context\n- Touches: local HTTP listener and request handling, browser assets served from the module, application entry point for web mode, game-state transitions shared with the terminal mode, new HTTP tests, and run documentation.\n- Does not touch: authentication, credential handling, production services, databases, deployment, external accounts, historical task evidence, or the existing `ttt` binary.\n- Requests may arrive concurrently while one game state is shared; the web handler must be race-free and must serialize state changes against the terminal game's rule functions.\n\n## Risk tier\n1\n\nRationale: the change adds a network-visible entry point and incremental game-state/logic changes on a developer machine; a mistake could silently change behavior but cannot touch identities, credentials, or entitlements, and there is no production deployment.\n\n## Review\n\nAn agent drafts this document. The declared spec-review Procedure then requires a human decision — or an explicitly delegated coordinator decision — tied to the reviewed artifact hashes. This v2 draft refines v1 against project evidence (`main.go`, `main_test.go`, `go.mod`, and the team gate scripts); no prior rejection feedback was available in this environment to incorporate. On rejection, this draft is revised in place using the feedback while preserving the original intent. A signature in this document does not approve the workflow."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791843543186}}
