)\n\nActually, let me reconsider. AC-5 (reuse existing functions) is something that should be inherent in each story, not a separate story. AC-6 (tests) should be part of each story's acceptance criteria, not a separate story. AC-7 (file layout) is also cross-cutting.\n\nLet me refine:\n\nUS-001: HTTP server serves the game UI and static assets (AC-1)\nUS-002: Web UI displays board and handles valid moves (AC-2, AC-5)\nUS-003: Web UI handles invalid moves and game-over states (AC-3, AC-5)\nUS-004: Reset functionality and responsive UI (AC-4)\nUS-005: Tests and documentation (AC-6, AC-7)\n\nThat covers all ACs. Let me write the plan now.\n\nLet me also consider what check.mjs requires: PLAN.md must include golangci|scripts/lint.sh and cover all AC-* criteria. The quality gates section must include the team lint gate.\n\nNow let me write the full PLAN.md."}}
