{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":10212,"output":434,"cacheRead":8192,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":13,"totalTokens":18838,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"The plan passes validation. Here's a summary of what was written to `/runtime/task/PLAN.md` addressing the rejected review feedback:\n\n### Correction 1 — Server-held state with `GET /state` (retrieval/refresh)\n- **Architecture section**: Declares a `GET /state` handler returning the full game state as JSON (board, currentPlayer, winner, gameOver).\n- **State retrieval paragraph**: Explains that page load/refresh calls `GET /state` to hydrate the UI from the server-held board without resetting it. A failed request leaves state unchanged.\n- **Testing strategy**: Includes `TestGetState_Initial`, `TestGetState_AfterMoves`, `TestGetState_RefreshHydration` (second tab/refresh sees identical state), `TestGetState_AfterFailedRequest`, and `TestGetState_NoResetOnRefresh`.\n- **US-001**: Covers `GET /state` hydration in acceptance criteria (after moves, after failed requests, multiple calls return same state).\n\n### Correction 2 — Single consistent web startup interface\n- Uses **`-addr` flag** consistently throughout: when absent, terminal mode (backward compatible default); when present (e.g., `-addr=localhost:8080`), HTTP server starts.\n- No conflicting subcommand vs addr-only alternatives. The `Alternatives considered` section explicitly documents the choice and the rejected subcommand approach.\n- Loopback default, address override via the flag.\n\n### Other requirements preserved\n- **Quality gates**: `bash /inputs/resources/team/scripts/build.sh`, `go test ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `bash /inputs/resources/team/scripts/lint.sh` — no separate lint stage.\n- **Risk tier recheck**: Tier 1 confirmed, unchanged.\n- **Spec ref**: `SPEC.md v2` matching the spec.\n- **Six sequenced stories** covering all AC-1 through AC-7, with US-001 (the riskiest — state retrieval) first."}}
